# CODEOWNERS for ai-toolkit
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more owners. The last
# matching line wins.

# Default owner for all files
* @lekman

# Release-please outputs, owned by the approver App alone. GitHub does not
# resolve an App as a code owner, so a file whose last matching line names only
# the App has no code owner, and the App's ordinary approval satisfies the
# review rule. Do not add a person or team to these lines: a resolvable owner
# brings the code-owner requirement back and the release pull request waits for
# a human. The globs match packages added later. The approve workflow's file
# check is the real control: it approves only when every changed file is one of
# these.
**/CHANGELOG.md                  @app/lekman-approver-bot
packages/**/package.json         @app/lekman-approver-bot
/.github/release-manifest.json   @app/lekman-approver-bot
